            make_q("Why do modern implementations of PCA use Singular Value Decomposition (SVD) on $X$ instead of computing the covariance matrix $X^T X$ directly?", ["SVD runs only on GPUs", "Computing $X^T X$ directly can square condition numbers, causing numerical instability and precision loss; SVD on $X$ is far more stable", "SVD eliminates the need for centering", "SVD produces fewer components"], 1, "SVD avoids computing $X^T X$ explicitly, providing superior numerical stability and precision on ill-conditioned data."),
            make_q("In SVD decomposition $X = U \\Sigma V^T$, which matrix contains the principal directions (eigenvectors of $X^T X$)?", ["The left singular vectors $U$", "The right singular vectors $V$ (or $V^T$ rows)", "The diagonal matrix $\\Sigma$", "The original matrix $X$"], 1, "The columns of $V$ (rows of $V^T$) are the right singular vectors, identical to the eigenvectors of the covariance matrix."),
